        "title": "How to customize or disable the touchscreen on the new MacBook Pro",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/09/how-to-customize-or-disable-the-touchscreen-on-the-new-macbook-pro-and-sidecar/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/11/Disable-MacBook-Touch-Display-FI.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A headlining feature of Apple’s new MacBook Pro with PROLED XDR Display is the long-awaited addition of a touchscreen. However, not everyone has been so thrilled about this addition. Here’s how you can turn it off.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"mac,macbook-pro,macos,tutorial\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1078104\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/09/how-to-customize-or-disable-the-touchscreen-on-the-new-macbook-pro-and-sidecar/#more-1078104\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
